es the condition $y(0)=-3$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-3{e}^{-x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "451f3842-16b6-5866-9651-73784c8644e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{4}-x+2}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345950} {:answer/id #uuid "58be30d8-ef50-5ef7-b5f3-523380bbc11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346113} {:answer/id #uuid "70a616da-72b0-575c-adfa-c326848aeb16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346340} {:answer/id #uuid "816eafe7-746e-5226-88e6-c6e7b7b43820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346482} {:answer/id #uuid "f1baeeb1-4f87-5895-9e67-a1a7e8844e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "816eafe7-746e-5226-88e6-c6e7b7b43820" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346482} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea329cec-2c85-5a3c-ae6a-b47fc15cd1cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348015}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49fb438b-3c89-5f2d-ad22-0703828a1cf7" :question/math-academy-id "q-79373" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(4{x}^{3}-1){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4{x}^{3}-1 \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4{x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{4}-x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{4}-1+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡C & =0 \\\\ C & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{-y}=4{x}^{3}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4}-x+1).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348224 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02894820-667a-5bb1-8d2d-4a0e95595d4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3{e}^{x}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345370} {:answer/id #uuid "1d756a9d-9a70-50be-87ba-3a12ce907a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2{e}^{{x}^{2}}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345607} {:answer/id #uuid "4914777d-f2b5-57b0-a44a-c23834802afd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2{e}^{x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345974} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d0bd7d-ae6a-5b73-af44-998074dd148c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}={e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346935} {:answer/id #uuid "d13ddd57-da35-5009-922f-44e87553a2f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d13ddd57-da35-5009-922f-44e87553a2f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347184} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0ce2963-49b7-5510-bb64-1ea4168634e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347969}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64550cf0-ae14-5b89-b54c-860d29b3d527" :question/math-academy-id "q-79425" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3} & =4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x(2+{y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the left-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2+{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3}) & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}} \\\\ 2+{y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{3} & =K{e}^{{0}^{2}}-2 \\\\ 1 & =K-2 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cad08fd0-a60c-5289-bfae-917d24b4cf51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-x-{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad08fd0-a60c-5289-bfae-917d24b4cf51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-x-{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373005} :answer-field/id #uuid "c01b75b0-e7f0-5237-8118-7d26642ee499" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1491d28-f486-5d5a-8bd7-310f4893ab88" :question/math-academy-id "q-355560" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(2)=-1.$\n\n|  | $y(x)=$ | $x$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}+1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =(4{x}^{-2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (4{x}^{-2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{y}^{-1} & =-4{x}^{-1}+x+C \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{4}{x}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving for $y$, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{4}{x}-x-C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{4-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{4-{x}^{2}-Cx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=-1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{4-{2}^{2}-C(2)} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{-2C} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{C} & =-1 \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{x}{4-x-{x}^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373526 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0ba7021-278a-5bfc-8d11-f00a3b63b0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}-4x+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373528} {:answer/id #uuid "0d863f80-974c-5fd0-9ba0-3d19bf8e3347" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373529} {:answer/id #uuid "22f9d7b5-6e34-51ba-a04a-13901fa9651e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}-4{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373530} {:answer/id #uuid "31b7712a-30c7-5b25-a8c1-60f541081385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{x}-2{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373531} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9220a2-0ad7-50c6-85ed-98e053e99e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc9220a2-0ad7-50c6-85ed-98e053e99e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373532} :answer-field/id #uuid "be7c8072-e10a-55ab-8358-3a565f0a6a95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373527}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fdc31d5-5a66-5e44-b1bd-e6668f2e6e14" :question/math-academy-id "q-104056" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x}=1$ that satisfies $y(0)=7.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x} & =1 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1-4x{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}-4x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({e}^{-x}-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=7$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =7 \\\\ -{e}^{-0}+2\\cdot {0}^{2}+C & =7 \\\\ C-1 & =7 \\\\ C & =8\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of ${e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4x{e}^{x}=1$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=7$ is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+8.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ddf8e77-1f92-52ca-ba0f-d3a0c8aeeddd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373535} {:answer/id #uuid "ddeef60e-4ec8-586c-a724-ac4e52f99051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373536} {:answer/id #uuid "eaeab17a-7de9-520a-be72-1e945c3a28b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+2e}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373537} {:answer/id #uuid "a08229ef-ec6b-54f8-8faf-e2cb18e885e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+2x-3+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373538} {:answer/id #uuid "9474dc52-92f4-5600-a6ca-5868d826ebe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{e{x}^{2}+e}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddeef60e-4ec8-586c-a724-ac4e52f99051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373536} :answer-field/id #uuid "493ad9d4-8aff-5cd3-bb25-1648834bbb25" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373534}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "52066178-466b-57ba-8963-0e5e66a7bec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-104057" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y}=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y} & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}-2x{e}^{-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(3{x}^{2}-2x){e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-2x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3}-{1}^{2}+C) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡C & =1 \\\\ C & =e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2x{e}^{-y}=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+e).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa22294c-97df-59d3-a2ef-bb723379bd93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404233} {:answer/id #uuid "05c76659-9ee2-5ea1-9921-4c61064bc47c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-2)/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404234} {:answer/id #uuid "d957c339-7d86-5b49-bfb4-f34772448576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{(2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-1)/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404235} {:answer/id #uuid "59acccda-8ad0-5671-8d3b-1eba77285637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404236} {:answer/id #uuid "08886f8e-1110-502c-b6b0-62359e9dd0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08886f8e-1110-502c-b6b0-62359e9dd0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404237} :answer-field/id #uuid "5399864b-fdb6-560a-bb1c-eadfa2e8485b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404232}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "177e97c5-b0fe-5fdf-abe1-80b42d3faf53" :question/math-academy-id "q-8306" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2yx+y{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(2x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =\\pm {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ y & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}/3} & =1 \\\\ K{e}^{4/3} & =1 \\\\ K & ={e}^{-4/3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2yx+y{x}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4/3}\\cdot {e}^{{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}/3}={e}^{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-4)/3}\\,.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}]}
